    "markdown": "## Lisbon: 7-day forecast\n\n**Best beach day: Tuesday.** It is the warmest day of the week at 26 °C and sunny. Monday (24 °C, sunny) is a good second choice, and Sunday (23 °C, sunny) works if you want to go at the weekend.\n\n| Day | Weather | High | Low |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Mon | ☀️ Sunny | 24 °C | 16 °C |\n| **Tue** | ☀️ **Sunny** | **26 °C** | **17 °C** |\n| Wed | ⛅ Partly cloudy | 23 °C | 16 °C |\n| Thu | 🌧️ Rain | 19 °C | 14 °C |\n| Fri | 🌧️ Rain | 18 °C | 13 °C |\n| Sat | ☁️ Cloudy | 20 °C | 14 °C |\n| Sun | ☀️ Sunny | 23 °C | 15 °C |\n\n### The week at a glance\n\n- **Start of the week is the best of it:** sunny and warming up to Tuesday's peak.\n- **Wednesday** is still pleasant at 23 °C, but clouds move in ahead of the rain.\n- **Thursday and Friday are wet** and the coolest days, with highs of 19 °C and 18 °C. Plan indoor things: museums, the Oceanário, a long lunch.\n- **The weekend recovers:** cloudy but dry on Saturday, then sunny again on Sunday.\n\n### For the beach\n\n- **Go Tuesday.** Bring sunscreen: a clear day in Lisbon means a high UV index even when the air feels mild.\n- The Atlantic is cool here, so the water will feel cold whatever the air temperature.\n- Evenings drop to 16–17 °C, so pack a light layer if you stay for sunset.\n",
